## 9. Inspect the OpenFlow flow tables

We ran:

Bash

```
for b in br-ryu-test s2 s3 s4 s5 s6 s7; do
    echo "========== $b =========="
    sudo ovs-ofctl -O OpenFlow13 dump-flows "$b"
done
```

This displayed two baseline rules per switch:

* A high-priority LLDP rule sending discovery packets to the controller.

* A priority-zero table-miss rule sending unmatched packets to the controller.

No explicit route-specific forwarding rules had been installed yet. The next stage is to create test endpoints, install rules for the primary path, verify traffic, and then test switching to the alternate path.

